---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for schools and colleges"
	description="Booking software for school and college ceramics departments: courses that run on your semester timetable, wheel time students book between classes, and firing queues for one or two kilns."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>A ceramics department that runs on the timetable.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of courses and a room full of students who want a wheel between
				classes. Kilnbook keeps the courses, the wheel calendar and the kiln shelf in one place, so
				nobody has to guard the sign-up sheet.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
			<h2>Three things a ceramics department juggles</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Courses on the semester timetable</h3>
					<p>
						Set up each course once as a fixed series, like Wheel 101 on Tuesdays, and let students
						book their seat. Waitlists fill a seat on their own when someone drops out, and
						instructors see their roster and mark attendance from the studio tablet.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheels between classes</h3>
					<p>
						Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks, so
						a free period becomes studio time instead of a race for the good wheel. You set how many
						hours they get and how far ahead they can book.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Firings for one or two kilns</h3>
					<p>
						Students log a piece when they set it on the bisque shelf. Each kiln has its own queue
						for bisque and glaze loads, a firing log records who loaded what, and students get a
						text when their work is ready for pickup.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Which plan?</h2>
		<p>
			Most departments with one or two kilns fit the Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, and class waitlists. If you only have one
			kiln, Starter covers it. Registered nonprofits and school ceramics programs get 30% off any
			plan. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns, so two kilns fit with room for a third. The Starter
					plan covers one kiln.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Is there a discount for schools?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we bring in our class lists from a spreadsheet?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your department off the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
